// Check that the BSC diagnostic reference (bsc-errors.md) can be generated from
// the real diagnostic metadata.  clang-tblgen fails if any BSC error/warning
// lacks BSCDiag<>/BSCOutOfScope, if codes collide within a feature, or if the
// Notes column refers to an unknown note, so a successful run validates the
// metadata; the FileCheck lines additionally pin down the document's shape.
//
// RUN: clang-tblgen -gen-bsc-diag-docs -DBSC \
// RUN:   -I%src_include_dir -I%src_include_dir/clang/Basic \
// RUN:   %src_include_dir/clang/Basic/Diagnostic.td -o %t.md
// RUN: FileCheck %s < %t.md

// CHECK: # BSC-Specific Diagnostics by Feature
// CHECK: ## OWN — owned
// CHECK: ## BOR — borrow
// CHECK: ## INIT — initialization
// CHECK: ## MISC — declaration / dispatch consistency
// CHECK: ## SZONE — safe zone
// CHECK: ## NONNULL — nonnull pointer
// CHECK: ## NULLABLE — nullable pointer
// CHECK: ## Summary
// CHECK: | **Total** | |
